**Key improvements:**
- Replaces 4 × 16×16 multipliers with 3 × 16×17 multipliers → ~20% less multiplier logic (the dominant area contributor)
- Keeps identical module interface, 1-cycle latency, and 1 output/cycle throughput
- Maintains bit-exact output (Gauss's method is exact over integers), so precision stays at 999.00
- The extra 17-bit pre-adders are cheap compared to the saved multiplier
